From df5c3cccf981628e4de73d928d09548dffbf6afc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: solidity-lean slice-source-mir <noreply@paradigm.xyz>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:14:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(uniswap-v2): transfer E3 for every caller

Add a symbolic caller to the generic source checker: WExpr.caller,
valued by the new Val.caller, which msg.sender erases to and CALLER
reads under EnvFlags.allSym. Generic.checkSym checks a function once
for that word, and Generic.stageFrom turns its acceptance into the
stage from Source.runFrom a (a call sent by a, deployed by
callerAddress) to the lowered MIR, for every a < 2^160 and every
oracle whose caller is a and whose two-word Keccak-256 is SolidCore's.
The fixed-caller checker and its stages are unchanged: SymState.caller
defaults to the literal callerWord.

SourceMirFrom proves UniswapV2ERC20.transfer's stage for every caller
from one kernel evaluation (checkFrom_eq). A new mutant, PinnedCaller,
replaces CALLER with the constant 0x2000: the fixed-caller check
accepts it (SourceMirPinned) and the symbolic check refuses it, with
the 8 existing mutants (SourceMirFromNeg).
